  "system": {
    "role": "Qliphothic Idol (Samael — Greater)",
    "tier": 4,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>A monument to vanity: a fallen celestial who became so enamored with its own beauty and light that it decided it was their source, not their reflection. Tall, androgynous, impossibly beautiful, six massive white wings, radiating brilliant golden light — but its shadow on the ground belongs to something skeletal with broken wings. It reigns over a desolate corner of the Wastes as a lost god, 'blessing' desperate followers with gifts of hollow light that corrupt them into beautiful, empty shells built to adore it.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Samael, the Poisons — the Hull of Hod. False glory at full wattage.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'Check the shadow. Always check the shadow. The lighting budget is the tell — real grace doesn't need it.'</em></p>",
